# Alejandro manifest envelope

Import AlejandroJsonFields from "./alejandro_json_fields.lg".
Import AlejandroProvenance from "./alejandro_provenance.lg".

## An AlejandroManifest has:
    a toolchain, which is Text.
    a historicalRevision, which is Text.
    a cases, which is Seq of Json.
    a rawDigest, which is Text.
## To alejandroManifestCounts (object: Json, rows: Seq of Json) -> Result of Bool and Text:
    Inspect jsonNoExtraKeys(object, ["translate", "degrade", "reject"]):
        When Err (failure):
            Return a new Err with error failure.
    Repeat for expectation in ["translate", "degrade", "reject"]:
        Let mutable declared be -1.
        Inspect alejandroIntField(object, expectation):
            When Ok (number):
                Set declared to number.
            When Err (failure):
                Return a new Err with error failure.
        Let mutable actual be 0.
        Repeat for row in rows:
            Inspect alejandroStringField(row, "expect"):
                When Err (failure):
                    Return a new Err with error failure.
                When Ok (value):
                    If value is equal to expectation:
                        Set actual to actual + 1.
        If declared is not equal to actual:
            Return a new Err with error "historical verdict counts disagree".
    Return a new Ok with value true.
## To alejandroManifestObject (object: Json, rawDigest: Text) -> Result of AlejandroManifest and Text:
    Let keys be ["corpus", "lean_toolchain", "logos_revision", "case_count", "verdict_counts", "cases"].
    Inspect jsonNoExtraKeys(object, keys):
        When Err (failure):
            Return a new Err with error failure.
    Let values be a new Seq of Text.
    Repeat for key in ["corpus", "lean_toolchain", "logos_revision"]:
        Inspect alejandroStringField(object, key):
            When Err (failure):
                Return a new Err with error failure.
            When Ok (value):
                Push value to values.
    If item 1 of values is not equal to "lean-to-logos-conformance":
        Return a new Err with error "unsupported corpus".
    If item 2 of values is not equal to "leanprover/lean4:v4.14.0":
        Return a new Err with error "unsupported original Lean toolchain".
    Let mutable count be 0.
    Inspect alejandroIntField(object, "case_count"):
        When Err (problem):
            Return a new Err with error problem.
        When Ok (number):
            Set count to number.
    Let mutable rows be a new Seq of Json.
    Inspect alejandroArrayField(object, "cases"):
        When Ok (caseRows):
            Set rows to caseRows.
        When Err (problem):
            Return a new Err with error problem.
    If count is not equal to 248:
        Return a new Err with error "the original corpus has 248 cases".
    If count is not equal to length of rows:
        Return a new Err with error "case count disagrees".
    Inspect jsonField(object, "verdict_counts"):
        When Err (failure):
            Return a new Err with error failure.
        When Ok (counts):
            Inspect alejandroManifestCounts(counts, rows):
                When Err (failure):
                    Return a new Err with error failure.
    Let decoded be a new AlejandroManifest with toolchain (item 2 of values) and historicalRevision (item 3 of values) and cases rows and rawDigest rawDigest.
    Return a new Ok with value decoded.
## To decodeAlejandroManifest (raw: Text) -> Result of AlejandroManifest and Text:
    Inspect alejandroStrictObject(raw):
        When Ok (object):
            Return alejandroManifestObject(object, alejandroRawDigest(raw)).
        When Err (failure):
            Return a new Err with error failure.
    Return a new Err with error "invalid manifest".
